{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n#define PAIR_TILE 32\\n\\n/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/* Allocation-free fallback with the original accumulation order. */\\nstatic void body_force_direct(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n    float fx = 0.0f;\\n    float fy = 0.0f;\\n    float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx;\\n    p[i].vy += dt*fy;\\n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/* Diagonal tiles retain the complete directed source loop, including self. */\\nstatic inline void accumulate_diagonal_tile(\\n    const float * restrict x,\\n    const float * restrict y,\\n    const float * restrict z,\\n    float * restrict fx,\\n    float * restrict fy,\\n    float * restrict fz,\\n    int first, int end) {\\n  for (int i = first; i < end; ++i) {\\n    const float tx = x[i];\\n    const float ty = y[i];\\n    const float tz = z[i];\\n    float ax = fx[i];\\n    float ay = fy[i];\\n    float az = fz[i];\\n\\n    for (int j = first; j < end; ++j) {\\n      float dx = x[j] - tx;\\n      float dy = y[j] - ty;\\n      float dz = z[j] - tz;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      ax += dx * inv_dist3;\\n      ay += dy * inv_dist3;\\n      az += dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    fx[i] = ax;\\n    fy[i] = ay;\\n    fz[i] = az;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Both tiles stay cache-resident. Rows accumulate ascending j values,\\n * while columns receive ascending i values. Reverse displacements are\\n * evaluated explicitly to preserve their signed-zero behavior.\\n */\\nstatic inline void accumulate_pair_tile(\\n    const float * restrict x,\\n    const float * restrict y,\\n    const float * restrict z,\\n    float * restrict fx,\\n    float * restrict fy,\\n    float * restrict fz,\\n    int first_i, int end_i, int first_j, int end_j) {\\n  for (int i = first_i; i < end_i; ++i) {\\n    const float tx = x[i];\\n    const float ty = y[i];\\n    const float tz = z[i];\\n    float ax = fx[i];\\n    float ay = fy[i];\\n    float az = fz[i];\\n\\n    for (int j = first_j; j < end_j; ++j) {\\n      const float sx = x[j];\\n      const float sy = y[j];\\n      const float sz = z[j];\\n      float dx = sx - tx;\\n      float dy = sy - ty;\\n      float dz = sz - tz;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      ax += dx * inv_dist3;\\n      ay += dy * inv_dist3;\\n      az += dz * inv_dist3;\\n\\n      float reverse_dx = tx - sx;\\n      float reverse_dy = ty - sy;\\n      float reverse_dz = tz - sz;\\n      fx[j] += reverse_dx * inv_dist3;\\n      fy[j] += reverse_dy * inv_dist3;\\n      fz[j] += reverse_dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    fx[i] = ax;\\n    fy[i] = ay;\\n    fz[i] = az;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\\n  if (n <= 0) {\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  if ((size_t)n > (size_t)-1 / (6 * sizeof(float))) {\\n    body_force_direct(p, dt, n);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  float *workspace = (float *)malloc((size_t)n * 6 * sizeof(float));\\n  if (workspace == NULL) {\\n    body_force_direct(p, dt, n);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  float * restrict x = workspace;\\n  float * restrict y = workspace + (size_t)n;\\n  float * restrict z = workspace + 2 * (size_t)n;\\n  float * restrict fx = workspace + 3 * (size_t)n;\\n  float * restrict fy = workspace + 4 * (size_t)n;\\n  float * restrict fz = workspace + 5 * (size_t)n;\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n    x[i] = p[i].x;\\n    y[i] = p[i].y;\\n    z[i] = p[i].z;\\n    if (!isfinite(x[i]) || !isfinite(y[i]) || !isfinite(z[i])) {\\n      free(workspace);\\n      body_force_direct(p, dt, n);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    fx[i] = 0.0f;\\n    fy[i] = 0.0f;\\n    fz[i] = 0.0f;\\n  }\\n\\n  const int blocks = n / PAIR_TILE + (n % PAIR_TILE != 0);\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp parallel if (blocks > 2)\\n#endif\\n  {\\n    /*\\n     * Pairs with the same block-index sum have disjoint bodies.\\n     * Increasing that sum visits every body's source blocks in order.\\n     * The implicit worksharing barrier separates successive waves.\\n     */\\n    for (int wave = 0; wave < 2 * blocks - 1; ++wave) {\\n      const int first_block = wave < blocks ? 0 : wave - blocks + 1;\\n      const int last_block = wave / 2;\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n#endif\\n      for (int block = first_block; block <= last_block; ++block) {\\n        const int other = wave - block;\\n        const int first_i = block * PAIR_TILE;\\n        const int first_j = other * PAIR_TILE;\\n        int count_i = n - first_i;\\n        int count_j = n - first_j;\\n        if (count_i > PAIR_TILE) {\\n          count_i = PAIR_TILE;\\n        }\\n        if (count_j > PAIR_TILE) {\\n          count_j = PAIR_TILE;\\n        }\\n        const int end_i = first_i + count_i;\\n        const int end_j = first_j + count_j;\\n\\n        if (block == other) {\\n          accumulate_diagonal_tile(x, y, z, fx, fy, fz, first_i, end_i);\\n        } else {\\n          accumulate_pair_tile(x, y, z, fx, fy, fz,\\n                               first_i, end_i, first_j, end_j);\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n#endif\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n      p[i].vx += dt*fx[i];\\n      p[i].vy += dt*fy[i];\\n      p[i].vz += dt*fz[i];\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  free(workspace);\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  /*\\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\\n   */\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(bodies);\\n\\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/nbody.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Wavefront-ordered, cache-resident body-pair tiles should reduce redundant distance evaluations while preserving each body's ascending-source accumulation order.\",\"notes\":\"Retains the original sqrt expression and direct fallback for non-finite positions or unavailable scratch storage. No commands or measurements were performed.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Replace eight-target full scans with 32-body pair tiles over compact SoA position and force storage.\",\"Parallelize disjoint tile pairs within barrier-separated anti-diagonal waves, preserving source-block order for every body.\",\"Share inverse distances across opposite interactions, explicitly recompute reverse displacements, and retain directed diagonal-tile calculations.\"]}"}}
